-- title:
--   Finiteness of the coefficient ring of a weight-two eigenform
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ be a natural number with $M \neq 0$, let $\varepsilon$ be a Dirichlet character modulo $M$ with values in $\mathbb{C}$, and let $h$ be a cusp form of weight $2$ for the congruence subgroup $\Gamma_1(M)$. Write $a_n(h)$ for the $n$-th coefficient of the $q$-expansion of $h$ (of width $1$). Assume that $h$ is an eigenform with character $\varepsilon$ in the sense used here, that is: $a_1(h) = 1$; for every prime $p \nmid M$ and every $n$, $a_{pn}(h) + \varepsilon(p)\, p^{2-1}\,[\,p \mid n\,]\,a_{n/p}(h) = a_p(h)\,a_n(h)$, where the bracket denotes the term $a_{n/p}(h)$ when $p \mid n$ and $0$ otherwise; for every prime $\ell \mid M$ and every $n$, $a_{\ell n}(h) = a_\ell(h)\,a_n(h)$; and $h$ has nebentypus $\varepsilon$, i.e. for every $\gamma \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ lying in $\Gamma_0(M)$ and every $\tau$ in the upper half-plane, $h(\gamma \cdot \tau) = \varepsilon(\gamma_{11} \bmod M)\,(\gamma_{10}\tau + \gamma_{11})^{2}\,h(\tau)$. Then the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathbb{C}$ generated by the set of all $a_n(h)$ for $n \in \mathbb{N}$ together with all values $\varepsilon(u)$ for $u \in (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ is a finite $\mathbb{Z}$-module.
--
--   This is the integrality and finiteness statement for the coefficient ring of a normalised weight-two Hecke eigenform with nebentypus: the ring generated by its $q$-expansion coefficients and the character values is an order-like finite $\mathbb{Z}$-module, so in particular all $a_n(h)$ are algebraic integers lying in a number field. It feeds the analysis of algebra homomorphisms out of the weight-two Hecke ring at Taylor–Wiles level, where an eigensystem must be realised inside a finite extension of a coefficient ring.
